                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The 111th Soul is incredibly short, with the entire game taking around 10–20 minutes even if you play through all three endings. There are no Steam achievements or Trading Cards either, which is a shame because the three endings, puzzles and other story milestones would have been perfect opportunities for them. The ending requirements are also rather ridiculous, with one ending depending on remembering trivial details from the house, and there have even been complaints about two of the endings being labelled incorrectly. It’s free now, but there simply isn’t enough here to make it particularly memorable.\n",
